      "block_role": "text_column",
      "reading_order": 7,
      "source_region_ids": [
        "PRM-G1-VIRAL-001-P006-R03-R"
      ],
      "crop_ids": [
        "P006-002-ATT-CROP-RIGHT"
      ],
      "evidence_predecessors": [
        "P006-READABLE-MAP-G1-VIRAL-001"
      ],
      "text_source_state": "human_verified",
      "text": "Age, offering countless sacrifices over the millennia. Only one of the 'Plague Monks' remains following a government raid on the island in the 1950s, the details of which have been diligently hidden from the public by the Italian government. The Plague Monk's only objective is to manifest Hastalÿk physically into the world, and spread its mutating corruption across the planet. Hastalÿk's ultimate plan is incomprehensible to mortals, but it certainly involves turning all life on Earth into itself through the spread of its Taint and absorbing all living things. To that end, it is vital to get the Investigators to witness the final sacrifice of the last Plague Monk at the Charnel Pit, and ideally become absorbed into the body of Hastalÿk themselves. After that, Hastalÿk will try to reach the water. Once it is able to touch the water, it bursts like a balloon to scatter its Taint to corrupt the nearby sea life, and eventually the world. Fortunately for the world, the Italian government has been watching the island, and indeed the live stream from the Spektral Krew. As soon as it becomes apparent that Hastalÿk is about to be released, the Italian military triggers its equivalent of the 'Innsmouth Protocol' and scrambles a squadron of jets to fire bomb the island, and end the vile corruption once and for all. Viral can be run in about four to eight hours depending on how the Keeper chooses to approach the scenario. Certain features are designed to be included or omitted as desired to speed up or slow down the game.",
